      "title": "Finding the Pivot Columns of a Matrix in Row Echelon Form"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/problem": "The row echelon form matrix $A$ is given below. What are the pivot columns of $A?$\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 8 & 4 & 7 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -7 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Remember that the pivots of a matrix in row echelon form are the first non-zero entries in each row of the matrix.\n\nWe can see that $A$ has $3$ pivots in the $1$st, $4$th, and $5$th columns:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 8 & 4 & 7 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -7 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$",
